.TH CHGRP 1 "February 2026" "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chgrp \- change group ownership
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chgrp
.RB [ \-R ]
.RB [ \-H | \-L | \-P ]
.RB [ \-fhv ]
.I group
.I file ...
.RS
.PP
.B chgrp
.RB [ \-R ]
.RB [ \-H | \-L | \-P ]
.RB [ \-fhv ]
.B \-r
.I file ...
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B chgrp
utility changes the group of each specified
.IR file .
The
.I group
argument may be a numeric group ID or a group name.
When
.B \-r
is specified,
.B chgrp
sets the group from a reference file (equivalent to
.B \-\-reference
in GNU).
.PP
.B chgrp
is equivalent to running
.B chown
with only the group portion specified (i.e., \fB:\fIgroup\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-R
Recursively change the group of directories and their contents.
.TP
.B \-H
When used with
.B \-R ,
follow symbolic links that appear on the command line, but do not follow
symbolic links encountered during traversal.
.TP
.B \-L
When used with
.B \-R ,
follow all symbolic links encountered during traversal.
.TP
.B \-P
Do not follow symbolic links during recursive traversal (default).
.TP
.B \-f
Suppress most diagnostics. Errors still cause a nonzero exit status.
.TP
.B \-h
Change the group of symbolic links themselves, rather than their targets.
.TP
.B \-r
Change the group using a reference file instead of a group operand.
.SH ERROR HANDLING
On per\-file failure,
.B chgrp
records the failure, continues processing remaining operands, and exits
with a nonzero status.
Error messages include the program name and target path unless
.B \-f
is specified.
.SH PORTABILITY NOTES
Setting group ownership on symbolic links is not supported on all platforms.
On platforms where it is unsupported,
.B \-h
fails for symbolic links with a clear diagnostic.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All requested group changes succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
One or more operations failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B chgrp staff file
Change the group of
.B file
to
.BR staff .
.TP
.B chgrp 100 file
Change the group of
.B file
to numeric group 100.
.TP
.B chown \-R staff /var/www
Recursively change group of
.B /var/www
to
.BR staff .
.TP
.B chgrp \-h users /usr/local/bin/link
Change group of the symbolic link
.B link
itself, not its target.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stat (2),
.BR lstat (2),
.BR fchown (2),
.BR chown (1),
.BR chmod (1)
